<title>SRI LANKA: Sri Lanka T-bill yields rise at weekly auction.</title>
<headline>Sri Lanka T-bill yields rise at weekly auction.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yields of three, six and 12-month Sri Lankan treasury bills rose at Wednesday's auction with twelve-month maturities oversubscribed, the Central Bank said.</p>
<p>		  bids received   bids accepted   avg yield</p>
<p>    3 months     3,105	     2,895	  17.64 (17.42)</p>
<p>    6 months	 181		 146	  17.57 (17.48)</p>
<p>   12 months     2,295	     1,510	  17.73 (17.52)</p>
<p>The bank said it purchased bills totalling 559 million rupees. NOTE - Bids in million rupees, yields in percent (previous week's yields in brackets). - Colombo newsroom 434319</p>
</text>
